reasoning_text:
Since d is odd, 2d is even (even times anything is even). Since n is even, 5n is also even (anything times even is even). Adding two even numbers gives an even number.

A

// Yeah this one's pretty straightforward - just had to remember that multiplying by an even number always gives you an even result, and even + even = even. Easy points.

